request.description:
Soroban RPC method `getEvents`. Set `endLedger` to a real closed ledger; this collection leaves it equal to startLedger as a placeholder.

Topic[0] is always an ScSymbol carrying the event name, and the payload is a contracttype-serialized struct. The six EphemeralAccount topics are:

  created     AccountCreated { creator, expiry_ledger }
  payment     PaymentReceived { amount, asset }         - first record_payment
  multi_pay   MultiPaymentReceived { asset, amount }    - subsequent record_payment
  swept_mul   SweepExecutedMulti { destination, payments }
  expired     AccountExpired { recovery_address, total_amount, reserve_amount }
  reserve     ReserveReclaimed { destination, amount, sweep_id, fully_reclaimed, remaining_reserve }

Per testnet/registry/event-topics.md. Note that `reserve` fires on every sweep and expiry with amount 0 once fully reclaimed, so event COUNT is not a proxy for value moved - filter on `amount`. And an event alone is not proof of a balance change.

Read-only RPC query: cannot change state.

